1
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:28,699
The Armour Research Reactor, located at the Illinois Institute of Technology in Chicago,

2
00:00:28,699 --> 00:00:36,100
is the world's first private nuclear reactor designed specifically for industrial research.

3
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:40,200
Construction costs for the reactor were borne jointly by the Armour Research Foundation,

4
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:48,240
which serves as owner and operator, and by 24 private industrial organizations.

5
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:52,700
This nuclear reactor was designed and built by Atomix International.

6
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:57,559
It opens an entirely new field of research for industry by providing a continuous on-the-spot

7
00:00:57,559 --> 00:01:07,760
source of neutrons, high-energy gamma rays, and radioisotopes. It is a

8
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:13,779
homogeneous solution type. The fuel is in the form of uranyl sulfate dissolved in

9
00:01:13,779 --> 00:01:23,240
distilled water and contained in a stainless steel spherical core. Cooling

10
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:27,020
for the core is provided by ten sections of stainless steel cooling coils

11
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:36,440
located within the core. The sections are connected in parallel and have a total length of 90 feet.

12
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:47,059
Distilled water serves as coolant and is continuously circulated through these coils.

13
00:01:47,059 --> 00:01:54,820
During core assembly, a series of tack wells was made to hold the two core sections rigidly in

14
00:01:54,819 --> 00:02:03,319
place. A shielded arc welder was then used to fuse the seam together without the use

15
00:02:03,319 --> 00:02:12,319
of filler rod. A stainless steel backup was drawn up into the weld, ensuring 100% penetration.

16
00:02:12,319 --> 00:02:22,919
Two additional weld passes made with filler rod completed the seam welding process. The

17
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:27,240
The core and fuel solution overflow assembly was inverted to facilitate installation of

18
00:02:27,240 --> 00:02:29,860
the graphite reflector.

19
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:35,800
The graphite sections were hand-cut to ensure a close fit.

20
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:40,860
After each block was individually marked and cut to size, assembly of the reflector was

21
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:47,520
fast and precise.

22
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:52,200
The tight fit around the core ensures a maximum of reflecting material in the most important

23
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:59,880
region for high reactor efficiency. A tube which extends through the center of the core

24
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:06,300
permits specimen exposure in the region of maximum flux density. Special safety features

25
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:20,360
are included to ensure completely safe operation in densely populated areas.

26
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:24,800
One example is this aluminum outer envelope, which encloses the core and its associated

27
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,800
piping.

28
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:37,280
If maintenance should be required, the entire core unit can be removed and reinstalled.

29
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:41,800
The neutron reflector consists of a stack of four-inch square graphite blocks which

30
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:46,480
have a high density and a very low percentage of boron.

31
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:52,940
The blocks were stacked in layers and surround the core assembly to form a reflector five

32
00:03:52,940 --> 00:04:03,759
feet high, five feet wide, and six and a half feet long.

33
00:04:03,759 --> 00:04:08,120
The exposure ports were plugged with wooden packing dowels prior to shipment to the reactor

34
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:09,800
site.

35
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:24,800
This assured proper alignment of the moderator blocks during transit.

36
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:31,800
Biological shielding is provided by a five foot thick wall of high density iron ore concrete.

37
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:43,120
A single bucket contains one cubic yard of dense concrete, which weighs over 6,000 pounds.

38
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:55,999
The dense concrete surrounds the reflector assembly and sub-pile room.

39
00:04:55,999 --> 00:04:59,999
The total weight of the reflector assembly is 10 tons.

40
00:05:05,999 --> 00:05:08,999
The instrumentation system which terminates in the control console

41
00:05:08,999 --> 00:05:12,999
consists principally of circuits to monitor and control reactor power

42
00:05:12,999 --> 00:05:16,999
and to display information on the performance of the gas handling and cooling systems.

43
00:05:16,999 --> 00:05:30,319
Four vertical control rods are provided for power level regulation and shutdown of the

44
00:05:30,319 --> 00:05:31,319
reactor.

45
00:05:31,319 --> 00:05:37,220
The rods are made of boron carbide encased in stainless steel.

46
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:43,100
They travel in sleeves extending through the spherical core.

47
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:47,499
As the rods are lowered into the core, the boron absorbs neutrons and the chain reaction

48
00:05:47,499 --> 00:05:49,020
cannot be maintained.

49
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:55,280
Thus, the reactor is stopped.

50
00:05:55,280 --> 00:06:03,120
By removing the rods, fission is increased and sustained at the desired level.

51
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:07,559
Reactor power level can be controlled either by automatic or manual operation of the control

52
00:06:07,559 --> 00:06:09,559
rods.

53
00:06:09,559 --> 00:06:16,100
To stop or scram the reactor, power to electromagnetic rod couplings is cut and the rods fall by

54
00:06:16,100 --> 00:06:19,720
gravity to the core.

55
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:24,459
The rods are also dropped automatically by the action of any of the reactor scram circuits

56
00:06:24,459 --> 00:06:32,079
or by power failure.

57
00:06:32,079 --> 00:06:36,160
Reactor fuel is urinal sulfate dissolved in light water.

58
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:46,860
The uranium is 88% enriched in the 235 isotope.

59
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:57,300
The solution water forms the moderator for slowing down the fission neutrons.

60
00:06:57,300 --> 00:07:01,720
An inherent safety feature acts to shut down the reactor in the event of an abnormal power

61
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:08,380
rise even if its mechanical devices should not function. This feature results from the

62
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:15,040
negative temperature coefficient and negative gas coefficient. Fuel solution temperature

63
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:21,020
increase is indicated by a shift from yellow to red. The negative temperature coefficient

64
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:26,620
results from the expansion of the fuel solution as its temperature rises. When the solution

65
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:32,059
expands, the reactor becomes less reactive due to its change in geometry and reactor

66
00:07:32,059 --> 00:07:39,059
power is decreased. The negative gas coefficient results from the radiolytic decomposition

67
00:07:39,579 --> 00:07:45,600
of the water, producing hydrogen and oxygen. These gases expand the solution to a subcritical

68
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:52,600
state which also shuts the reactor down. If a power surge should ever be great enough,

69
00:07:56,620 --> 00:08:01,620
It would force a portion of the solution into the overflow chamber above the core.

70
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:04,620
It would leave the reactor in a sub-critical state

71
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:11,620
and the appropriate corrective action could be taken.

72
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:14,620
The solution would then drain slowly back to the core

73
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:24,620
and the reactor could be started once again.

74
00:08:24,620 --> 00:08:32,580
The shutdown mechanism just demonstrated will operate only in the event that all mechanical control and safety systems should not function.

75
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:46,779
The horizontal thermal column is five feet square and is shielded by a motor driven dense concrete door.

76
00:08:46,779 --> 00:08:59,299
The door weighs 40,000 pounds and has limit switches to stop the in or out travel.

77
00:08:59,299 --> 00:09:06,159
Large specimens as well as special test equipment can be placed in this exposure facility.

78
00:09:06,159 --> 00:09:11,259
In this experiment, the reactor is being used to study the effects of slow neutron bombardment

79
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:18,259
on a laboratory test moderator.

80
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:27,700
A fast neutron beam is also available when graphite stringers are removed from the center

81
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:34,700
of the thermal face.

82
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:41,700
With the test equipment in place, the reactor is ready for start-up.

83
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:50,700
Since radioactive materials are present in the reactor and are handled in the experiments,

84
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:55,700
a positive means for controlling the atmosphere in the reactor room is provided.

85
00:09:55,700 --> 00:10:02,700
The concrete room walls are coated with the plastic paint to prevent the passage of gases.

86
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:07,700
Specially designed gas-tight doors seal the reactor room.

87
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:23,700
From the control console, the operator monitors and controls the complete operation of the reactor.

88
00:10:24,700 --> 00:10:28,700
A check is made of the various instruments which display control rod position,

89
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:33,320
position, cooling system temperatures, gas handling system pressures and other

90
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:40,320
information required for efficient and safe reactor operation. As control rods

91
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:46,700
are withdrawn from the core, the fission chain reaction begins.

92
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:51,800
Technicians in the control room and on the reactor floor talk with each other

93
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:56,540
over an intercommunication system. In this way information presented on

94
00:10:56,539 --> 00:11:00,799
monitoring equipment set up adjacent to the reactor may be instantly and

95
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:08,719
continuously compared with control console data the heavy concrete

96
00:11:08,719 --> 00:11:13,219
biological shielding which surrounds the reactor permits personnel to remain in

97
00:11:13,219 --> 00:11:19,099
the reactor room during operation there are 18 tube type exposure facilities in

98
00:11:19,099 --> 00:11:23,059
the reactor consisting of metal tubes which extend through the concrete shield

99
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:29,360
to the immediate vicinity of the core. Each tube facility is equipped with a

100
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:39,940
graphite reflector plug and a dense concrete and steel shielding plug. Access

101
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:44,560
is gained to the region of maximum flux density through a central tube facility

102
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:52,740
which extends through the center of the core. Nuclear reactors have a variety of

103
00:11:52,740 --> 00:12:03,820
of practical applications.

104
00:12:03,820 --> 00:12:13,980
A complete listing of the many uses of radioactivity in radiation would run into the thousands.

105
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:18,659
Among the current applications is the development of new chemical processes and products.

106
00:12:18,659 --> 00:12:25,620
Here, a radioactive carbon isotope is being transformed from radioactive carbon dioxide

107
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:29,980
gas to a radioactive organic liquid.

108
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:38,839
This is a useful tool for research on plastics, synthetic fabrics, and pharmaceutical products.

109
00:12:38,839 --> 00:12:44,579
A laboratory technique known as activation analysis is coming into widespread usage.

110
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:50,040
Impurities too small to be detected by chemical or spectroscopic analysis can be detected

111
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:57,520
by irradiating a small sample of material, and then measuring the activity thus produced.

112
00:12:57,520 --> 00:13:06,340
By studying the gamma energies emitted, impurities present are identified and analyzed.

113
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:11,020
The effects of radiation on transistors and semiconductors is being studied.

114
00:13:11,019 --> 00:13:16,759
A transistor which has been irradiated in a reactor undergoes a series of stability tests.

115
00:13:18,019 --> 00:13:24,579
Research of this type plays an important part in the development of new materials and techniques for electronic applications.

116
00:13:29,759 --> 00:13:36,279
In the field of botany and agriculture, extensive research is being conducted with the aid of radioisotopes.

117
00:13:36,279 --> 00:13:42,079
Here, an analysis is made on the absorption of radioactive phosphorus into the structural

118
00:13:42,079 --> 00:13:45,100
components of tomato plants.

119
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:51,240
This is a study of drought resistance, protein formation, and growth itself, as affected

120
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:54,079
by water shortage.

121
00:13:54,079 --> 00:14:05,819
Without the aid of radioisotopes, many phases of this work would be impossible.

122
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:09,740
Radioisotopes are also playing an increasingly important part in modern medicine.

123
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:14,040
This patient is being given a diagnostic test of the thyroid.

124
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:20,860
Before this test, she drank a solution containing a tracer amount of radioactive iodine.

125
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:27,760
A scintillation counter above the area of the thyroid will pick up the extremely low-level gamma rays

126
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:30,960
emitted by the iodine, now localized in the thyroid.

127
00:14:35,820 --> 00:14:40,780
The impulses from the scintillation counter are sent to a recording chart to

128
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:46,040
indicate exactly how the thyroid is functioning. Prior to the use of

129
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:50,980
radioisotopes, such a diagnosis was difficult and frequently required

130
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:53,480
surgery.

131
00:14:56,180 --> 00:15:01,120
In addition to present-day applications, many future benefits from research

132
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:06,919
reactors can be anticipated. By providing an immediate source of neutrons, gamma

133
00:15:06,919 --> 00:15:12,279
rays and radioisotopes, this nuclear reactor brings to industry a new and

134
00:15:12,279 --> 00:15:18,499
valuable research tool. As the focal point of an intensive research program

135
00:15:18,499 --> 00:15:23,399
stimulated by the enthusiastic support of private enterprise, this reactor

136
00:15:23,399 --> 00:15:53,340
establishes a new concept in the rapidly expanding field of industrial research.
